<title>BELGIUM: EU sceptical about grain crop data.</title>
<headline>EU sceptical about grain crop data.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The latest European Union cereal crop estimates put to the EU cereals management committee on Thursday exceeded 200 million tonnes and seem to be exaggerated, a European Commission official said.</p>
<p>&quot;The Commission simply did not believe the figures which were considerably over the 200 million mark and has postponed a decision on its internal overview of the 1996/97 harvest,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>Commission officials are recommending that no final estimate should be made until the Swedish crop forecasts are available.</p>
<p>&quot;Crop forecasts are extremely high and it is likely that the final estimate will reflect this but it is still too soon to decide on a global figure,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>In Paris, sources close to the EU executive said on Thursday that figures provided by member states would total a minimum of 195 million tonnes and might not be totally reliable.</p>
</text>
